      "deviations": [
        "8-GPU smoke could NOT be confirmed at the time of writing because 4 of the 8 GPUs (3,5,6,7) are saturated (44-78 GB) by co-tenant processes, so NVSHMEM's internal-NCCL team setup / symmetric-heap reservation fails on those GPUs. The 8-GPU path DID pass once earlier in the session when more GPUs were free; the cross-GPU bring-up is otherwise proven correct on 2 and 4 GPUs (bit-exact all-reduce). This is a resource/co-tenancy blocker, NOT a defect in the pybind. Re-run the 8-GPU smoke when all 8 GPUs are <1 GB used.",
        "Container blocker (scoped + mitigated, not a defect): the RunPod container forbids NVLink-SHARP multicast cuMemMap (cuMemMap of the MC group fails with CUDA 'invalid argument') — the SAME class of restriction as the documented ncu perf-counter blocker. This hits BOTH NCCL's NVLS path and NVSHMEM's. Mitigation: NVSHMEM_DISABLE_NVLS=1 and NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0, set automatically at module import in grokking_optimizers/nvshmem_bringup_ext.py and at the top of tests/hw/nvshmem_smoke.py. With these set the UID+P2P/NVLink path works.",
        "Linked the EXPORTED nvshmemx_hostlib_init_attr / nvshmemx_hostlib_finalize entry points instead of the header-inline nvshmem_init() / nvshmem_finalize() wrappers, because the inline wrappers call nvshmemi_init_thread / nvshmemi_finalize which are NOT exported by libnvshmem_host.so.3 (undefined-symbol at import). Functionally equivalent (the inline only adds a version stamp that NVSHMEMX_INIT_ATTR_INITIALIZER already sets).",
        "team_split_strided returns a fresh team id (observed handle=7) even for the whole-world pure-TP split rather than NVSHMEM_TEAM_WORLD (0); this is correct NVSHMEM behaviour and the launcher reads the handle from CommCtx.tp_comm_handle, so the is_pure_tp_world fast-path in the plan is only an optimization hint, not a correctness requirement.",
        "Did not run the vit_tc / mamba_tc byte-identity gates (only decoder_tc) to conserve GPU hours under co-tenant pressure; my changes touch no .cu file, no kernel header, and no committed .cpp built into _ops (the new TU is *.cpp, and setup.py globs only *.cu under csrc/fused/sm_90), so all three model paths are byte-identical by construction and _ops imports unchanged."
      ],
      "gate_output_tail": "decoder_tc gate: 19 passed, 1 warning in 141.14s\n\n2-GPU smoke (GPUs 0,1): PASS\n  nvshmem_init OK: world_pe=0 world_npes=2\n  team_split OK: handle=7 local_pe=0 n_pes=2\n  nvshmem_malloc OK: floats=409,600\n  all-reduce: expected=3.0 got=[3.0,3.0] per-rank-ok=True\n  PASS: UID bootstrap + team split + symmetric malloc + cross-rank all-reduce correct across 2 GPUs.\n\n4-GPU smoke (GPUs 0,1,2,4, ctas-per-pe=16 -> flagship-class heap 6,553,600 floats=26.2MB): PASS\n  nvshmem_init OK: world_pe=0 world_npes=4\n  team_split OK: handle=7 local_pe=0 n_pes=4\n  nvshmem_malloc OK: floats=6,553,600\n  all-reduce: expected=10.0 got=[10.0,10.0] per-rank-ok=True\n  PASS: cross-rank all-reduce correct across 4 GPUs.\n\n8-GPU smoke: PASSED once early (expected=36 got 36 on all 8 ranks); now blocked by co-tenant GPU saturation (GPUs 3,5,6,7 at 44-78GB) -> NVSHMEM internal-NCCL team_internal.cpp:706 CUDA error / cuMemAlloc OOM on the loaded GPUs.",
      "summary": "Delivered the real host NVSHMEM TP-team bring-up that Python could not drive before. Key files (all absolute):\n\n- /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_89f9a418-f9d-2/csrc/fused/sm_90/nvshmem_bringup_pybind.cpp — the new host-only pybind TU. Compiled against the REAL NVSHMEM 3.7 headers (no ABI guessing) and linked against libnvshmem_host.so.3. Exposes: get_uniqueid / uniqueid_size / init_with_uniqueid (NVSHMEMX_INIT_WITH_UNIQUEID via nvshmemx_set_attr_uniqueid_args + the EXPORTED nvshmemx_hostlib_init_attr) / team_split_strided / malloc_symmetric_heap / tp_allreduce_smoke / barrier_world / finalize + introspection. NOT collected into _ops (setup.py globs *.cu; this is *.cpp), so the SingleGPU/default path stays byte-identical.\n\n- /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_89f9a418-f9d-2/grokking_optimizers/nvshmem_bringup_ext.py — the live driver: JIT-builds the pybind (links the versioned soname via ld -l:libnvshmem_host.so.3, adds CUDA include/lib), runs the three-step bring-up (init over the UID broadcast + team split + collective symmetric malloc), returns the resolved CommCtx fields, and sets the NVLS-disable container knobs.\n\n- /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_89f9a418-f9d-2/tests/hw/nvshmem_smoke.py — the torchrun cross-GPU smoke (UID init + team split + symmetric malloc + a tiny team all-reduce asserting cross-rank correctness).\n\n- /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_89f9a418-f9d-2/tuning/flagship_distributed.py — replaced the TPBootstrapBlocked stub in run_rank with the real bringup_tp_team_live call (fixed-length 128-byte UID broadcast over the NCCL PG), and import the ext module before init_process_group so the NVLS knobs apply to NCCL too.\n\nGATES: decoder_tc byte-identity gate 19 passed; 2-GPU and 4-GPU smokes PASS bit-exact (4-GPU run exercised the flagship-class 26.2MB symmetric heap). 8-GPU passed once when GPUs were free and is currently blocked only by co-tenant GPU saturation (resource, not the pybind). The genuine wildcard — host NVSHMEM bring-up from Python with no nvshmem binding and no MPI/PMI — is solved via the UID-plugin path; the only container blocker (NVLS multicast cuMemMap, same class as the ncu blocker) is precisely scoped and auto-mitigated with NVSHMEM_DISABLE_NVLS=1 / NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0."
