      "deviations": [
        "The prompt framed (1) as recalibrating only the SSM B-projection bias group (B_bias/Bhat_bias/C_bias/etc). Measuring the bf16-vs-fp64 floor at the exact gate config (B=128, seed=5) showed FIVE tensors exceed the 0.08 base, not just the biases: layers.0.mixer.B_bias (0.1546), layers.0.mixer.C_norm.weight (0.1415), tok.weight (0.0994), layers.0.mlp.down_proj.weight (0.0875), layers.0.mixer.Bhat_bias (0.0859). To honor the no-suppression discipline (gate each tensor to its measured floor), the elevated tol group was widened to the full complex SSM B/C stream (the *_bias AND BCNorm *_norm.weight tensors), the token embedding, and the SwiGLU down_proj dW — all B*S-token-reduced sign-cancelling grads. This is broader than the prompt's literal bias-only group but is the faithful application of the same discipline (the B_bias floor of 0.1546 matches the prompt's stated 0.1546 exactly).",
        "Used a single elevated tol of 0.30 (~1.94x the measured 0.1546 max floor, inside the prompt's 1.5-3x headroom band) rather than per-tensor distinct tols, mirroring the decoder's two-tier (0.08/0.15) scheme. Added a STRONGER per-tensor no-suppression witness on top: k-vs-bf16 must stay within 3x each tensor's OWN measured bf16-vs-fp64 floor + base, so a real bug (k-vs-bf16 >> floor) is caught even under the loose 0.30 tol.",
        "For (2), chose the documented @pytest.mark.skip option (not the adapt option). Adapting to a scalar full-grad-partial dW witness would require a new C++ partial-dump binding (the kernel comment states the dW lives in the per-CTA full-grad partial, not a separable operand region); the 4 tensor-core GEMM dWs are already validated end-to-end by the keystone grad-parity test's per-tensor floor witness, so the isolation hook's coverage is subsumed, not lost.",
        "Had to remove a stale torch JIT build-lock baton (~/.cache/torch_extensions/.../mega_mamba_real_adamw_tc/lock) left by an earlier killed build; it was causing every module load to hang in file_baton.wait(). This is a transient cache artifact, not a repo change."
      ],
      "gate_output_tail": "[mbtc] loss kernel=4.733776 bf16-oracle=4.734036 rel=5.51e-05\n  grad layers.0.mixer.B_bias        k-vs-bf16 1.547e-1  bf16-vs-fp64 1.546e-1  tol 0.3  <hi-cancel>\n  grad layers.0.mixer.C_norm.weight k-vs-bf16 1.415e-1  bf16-vs-fp64 1.415e-1  tol 0.3  <hi-cancel>\n  grad tok.weight                   k-vs-bf16 9.940e-2  bf16-vs-fp64 9.939e-2  tol 0.3  <hi-cancel>\n  grad layers.0.mlp.down_proj.weight k-vs-bf16 8.750e-2 bf16-vs-fp64 8.750e-2  tol 0.3  <hi-cancel>\n[mbtc] STRUCTURAL: layer0 proj-weight mean rel=4.298e-02  layer1=3.523e-02\n[mbtc] bf16-floor (bf16faithful vs fp64) max over all grads = 1.546e-01\n.s[mbtc] determinism A/A/A: loss 4.68193722 bit-identical, grad max-Δ=0\n.[mbtc] trajectory: loss[0]=4.6936 loss[49]=0.0012 min=0.0012\n.[mbtc] step-time TC=44.603ms scalar=8.892ms ratio=0.20× (informational)\n.\n4 passed, 1 skipped, 1 warning in 10.58s\nPYTEST_EXIT=0",
      "summary": "Fixed the 2 pre-existing Mamba TC test failures in /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_89f9a418-f9d-3/tests/hw/test_mamba_tc.py using the decoder's floor-calibrated discipline. Gate now: 4 passed, 1 skipped (PYTEST_EXIT=0).\n\n(1) test_tc_single_step_grad_parity: I independently measured the bf16-vs-fp64 floor at the EXACT gate config (B=128, seed=5) and confirmed the prompt's premise — layers.0.mixer.B_bias floor = 0.15463 (matches the prompt's 0.1546), and the kernel rides it (k-vs-bf16 1.547e-1 == bf16-vs-fp64 1.546e-1, i.e. correct, not a bug). Measurement also revealed the high-cancellation set is broader than the biases alone: it includes the complex SSM B/C BCNorm weights (C_norm.weight floor 0.1415), the token embedding (0.0994), and the SwiGLU down_proj dW (0.0875) — all B*S-token sums with sign cancellation. Added an elevated per-tensor tol of 0.30 (~1.94x the measured 0.1546 max floor, inside the 1.5-3x band) for that group via a new _is_high_cancel() classifier, kept 0.08 for all others (verified every non-elevated tensor's floor < 0.08). Added a stricter no-suppression witness: each grad's k-vs-bf16 must stay within 3x its OWN measured bf16 floor + base (a real bug, k-vs-bf16 ~1 >> floor, trips this even under the loose tol). Retained the structural layer0~=layer1 witness (measured 4.30e-2 vs 3.52e-2).\n\n(2) test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands: skipped via @pytest.mark.skip with a full documented reason — the wgmma output-stationary stored-bf16-acts dump (tc_dump_outproj_operands) is hard-obsoleted (TORCH_CHECK(false)) on the Mamba-3 scalar SSM path at csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_mamba_real_adamw_tc.cu:148; the dW lives in the per-CTA full-grad partial with no separable acts region. Its dW coverage is subsumed by the keystone test's per-tensor floor witness. Also updated the _main() direct-run path to print [SKIP] instead of calling the obsolete hook.\n\nScope: ONLY tests/hw/test_mamba_tc.py changed (86 insertions, 12 deletions). No kernel or model source touched — the SingleGPU/default path and the 3 model byte-identity gates are unaffected; gfx942/tpu untouched. Dirty .pyc and .pytest_cache files were restored with git checkout before committing. Relevant file: /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_89f9a418-f9d-3/tests/hw/test_mamba_tc.py"
